Message-ID: <0f47e2f1d4d2778136e764a1cb78b80d@xs4all.nl>

On 2019-08-26 09:04, Andreas Tille wrote:
>> Upstream is aware of the issue, see:
>> 
>>  https://github.com/r-spatial/lwgeom/issues/42
> 
> I have rebuild r-cran-lwgeom 0.1-7-1 with the recent proj in unstable.
> Here is a grep from the build log:
> 
> [...]
> 
> The package builds fine.  Do you agree that I can close the bug?

Yes. As you can see in the upstream issue, 0.1-7 fixes the FTBFS with 
PROJ 6 by defining -DACCEPT_USE_OF_DEPRECATED_PROJ_API_H among other 
changes.

This is sufficient for now, until the transition to PROJ 7 (sometime 
after March 2020) which will remove proj_api.h.

Kind Regards,

Bas


